 "_note": "Fixed limit thread gauges for Unified threads: the gauge maker's X tolerance on pitch diameter and which product limit each gauge member is made to. Tables transcribed on 2026-11-12. The X tolerances are those of ASME B1.2 as two gauge makers print them; the standard itself was not read.",
 "sources": {
  "TC_TOL": {
   "publisher": "Thread Check Inc.",
   "title": "Product catalogue, p. 52, 'Gage tolerances' (W tolerance and X tolerance tables)",
   "url": "https://www.threadcheck.com/technical-documents/gage-tolerances-pg52.pdf",
   "accessed": "2026-11-12",
   "note": "Gauge maker. X tolerance on pitch diameter by threads per inch for four diameter ranges (to 1 1/2 in, to 4 in, to 8 in, to 12 in), with lead, half angle and major and minor diameter tolerances. The text of the PDF runs the columns together; each row was placed by counting its values and agrees with Royal Oak Gage where both print a cell. The row printed '4 1/4' in the X table is 4 1/2 (as in the W table and in Royal Oak's)."
  },
